<rtept lat="51.3680376099" lon="-1.7614584707">
<time>2025-07-30T08:37:06Z</time>
<name>Giant's Grave to Sunnyhill Lane</name>
<desc><![CDATA[Continue along the path to pass the trig point (on the right) of Oare Hill. At 250m above sea level, this place is a great spot for enjoying the expansive views. You will see the village of Oare in the valley ahead. Within the village is an obvious mansion house, Oare House, built around 1740 then remodelled in the early 1920s by Portmeirion architect Clough Williams-Ellis.

Keep ahead on the obvious path following the line of the fence on the right. The path leads you fairly steeply downhill towards the village of Oare. The path swings steadily left and leads you down to a stile in the field corner. Cross the stile, bear left to follow the fence line on the left and, where the fence steps back, keep ahead in the same direction across the field. 

Cross the stile in the bottom fence line to reach a crossroads with a bridleway. Cross over the bridleway and go straight ahead into the field opening opposite. Follow the field edge grass track as it bends right and then left. At the far end of the field you will pass out through an open gateway to reach a junction with Sunnyhill Lane.]]></desc>
