<rtept lat="51.3542100000" lon="-1.7507700000">
<time>2025-07-30T08:36:05Z</time>
<name>Bridge 112 to West Wick House</name>
<desc><![CDATA[Do not pass under this bridge, instead fork right through the open gateway immediately before it. Pass through the stone clearing and then turn left along the lane, passing over the canal bridge. Follow this quiet lane ahead, taking care of any occasional traffic. 

In the winter you may be rewarded with large flocks of starlings chattering away in the trees. After the right-hand bend, you will get a good view ahead of the Marlborough Downs ridge that you will be climbing shortly (don't worry, the views will make it worthwhile!).

At the first road junction keep straight ahead on the dead-end branch signed to West Wick. Follow the lane ahead, which passes West Wick Cottages on the right and then becomes a tarmac bridleway. At the next junction, keep ahead again on the bridleway (now a track with a grassy centre) passing a concrete outbuilding on the right. Further along you will pass West Wick House on the left with a pretty shepherd's hut within the grounds. ]]></desc>
